# MODULE sixteen bit program counter ledger
# PURPOSE index admitted Brainfuck commands for a future scalable dispatcher
# INPUT chunks begin with a count byte and the exact command bytes
# INPUT a zero count closes the supplied source stream
# OUTPUT each admitted command as two little endian index bytes and one opcode byte
# OUTPUT a final three byte marker with all ones index
# OUTPUT marker opcode zero means eligible and all ones means reject
# TAPE low and high index counters use cells two and three
# TAPE physical input closure and annotated grammar are independently required
# SAFETY records are provisional until terminal marker and verified host closure
# LIMITATION at most sixty five thousand five hundred thirty five commands
# LIMITATION this indexed ledger does not execute guest instructions

